o (col AY DIC_Calculations file).',1,'2020-10-26 12:05:25','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(34,31,'Gases','Dissolved inorganic carbon isotope - Calc. [‰]','d13C_DIC','‰','d13C_DIC_avg','d13C_DIC_std',NULL,'sdPlot','Water ?13C?DIC isotopic composition from two replicates (A and B or 1 and 2). Calculated from Picarro output (Delta 13CO2 col AI_Calculation file).',1,'2020-10-26 12:05:25','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(35,32,'Ecosystem properties','Total suspended solids - Lab [mg/L]','TSS_dry_weight','mg/L','TSS_dry_weight_mgL',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Particles larger than 2 microns that are suspended in the water column. Measured in the laboratory by filtration of a water sample.',1,'2020-10-26 12:05:25','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(36,33,'Ecosystem properties','Ashed free dry mass - Lab [mg/L]','AFDM','mg/L','AFDM_mgL',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Inorganic portion of the TSS. Measured in the laboratory after ashing the filtered total suspended solids at 450°C for 4 hours.',1,'2020-10-26 12:05:25','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(37,34,'Ecosystem properties','Chlorophyll a - Lab [µg/L]','Chla_avg','µg/L','Chla_acid_avg_ugm2','Chla_acid_sd_ugm2',NULL,'sdPlot','Specific form of chlorophyll used in oxygenic photosynthesis. Measured in the laboratory from rock samples.',1,'2020-10-26 12:05:25','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(38,35,'Ecosystem properties','Benthic ashed free dry mass - Lab [g/m2]','benthic_AFDM_avg','g/m2','benthic_AFDM_avg_gm2','benthic_AFDM_sd_gm2',NULL,'sdPlot','Refers to the biomass present after filtration of the biofilm covering the sampled rocks. Measured in the laboratory.',1,'2020-10-26 12:05:25','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(39,36,'Gases','Methane Check','CH4','uM','CH4_umol_L_avg','CH4_umol_L_sd',NULL,'sdPlot',NULL,1,'2021-06-07 16:33:35','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(40,37,'Gases','Methane Isotopes - CHECK','iCH4','-','lab_co2_ich4_A,lab_co2_ich4_B',NULL,NULL,'multiPlot',NULL,1,'2021-06-07 16:47:28','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(41,38,'Ecosystem properties','Chla','Chla_noacid_avg_ugm2','ug/m2','Chla_noacid_avg_ugm2',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot',NULL,1,'2021-09-22 15:14:11','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(42,39,'Dissolved organic carbon','Biological index','BIX','-','BIX',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot',NULL,1,'2021-10-22 13:48:43','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(43,40,'Dissolved organic carbon','Peak B','B','-','B',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Protein-like material (Cobble, 1996)',1,'2021-10-25 15:51:48','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(44,41,'Dissolved organic carbon','Peak T','T','-','T',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Protein T, representing protein-like component.',1,'2021-10-25 15:53:21','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(45,42,'Dissolved organic carbon','Peak A','A','-','A',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Humic-like fluorescence stimulated by UV excitation, indicating the presence of humic substances and recent materials (Cobble, 1996).	',1,'2021-10-25 15:54:44','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(46,43,'Dissolved organic carbon','Peak M','M','-','M',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Peak M, indicating marine humic-like component.	',1,'2021-10-25 15:55:07','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(47,44,'Dissolved organic carbon','Peak C','C','-','C',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Humic-like fluorescence stimulated by visible excitation and indicating the presence of humic substances (Cobble, 1996).	',1,'2021-10-25 15:55:45','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(48,45,'Dissolved organic carbon','The fluorescence index','FI','-','FI',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','The fluorescence index (FI) distinguishes DOM derived from terrestrial sources (degraded plant and soil organic matter; lower values) vs. microbial sources (extracellular release and leachate from bacteria and algae; higher values) (McKnight et al. 2001; Cory et al. 2007, 2010). FI values in natural waters typically range between 1.2 and 1.8 (e.g., Jaffe et al. 2008; Wilson and Xenopoulos 2009; Cory et al. 2010; Carpenter et al. 2013; Helms et al. 2013; Fleck et al. 2014).',1,'2021-10-25 15:56:34','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(49,46,'Dissolved organic carbon','Humification index','HIX','-','HIX',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','The humification index (HIX) is an indicator of source, diagenesis and sorptive capacity (Zsolnay et al. 1999; Ohno 2002) and informs about the decrease of the ratio of hydrogen to carbon as humification of DOM proceeds, shifting the emission spectra of the fluorescing molecules toward the longer wavelengths with higher values indicating an increasing degree of humification. HIX values commonly range between 0.6 and 0.9 (e.g., Ohno 2002; Chen et al. 2011; Fleck et al. 2014)',1,'2021-10-25 15:57:14','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(50,47,'Dissolved organic carbon','a254','a254','-','a254',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','The a254 indicates humic and aromatic compounds in water (Abbt-Braun et al. 2004)',1,'2021-10-25 15:57:45','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(51,48,'Dissolved organic carbon','Specific ultraviolet absorbance','SUVA','-','SUVA',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','The specific ultraviolet absorbance (SUVA) provides a proxy of the hydrophilicity and hydrophobicity of all aromatic dissolved organic carbon (White et al. 1997)',1,'2021-10-25 15:58:26','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(52,49,'Dissolved organic carbon','a300','a300','-','a300',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','The absorption coefficient at 300 nm (a300).	',1,'2021-10-25 15:58:44','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(53,50,'Dissolved organic carbon','E2/E3','E2_E3','-','E2_E3',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Ratio between the absorption coefficient at 250 nm (a250) and the absorption coefficient at 365 nm (a365). Estimates the relative composition of autochthonous vs. terrestrial DOM.',1,'2021-10-25 15:59:21','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(54,51,'Dissolved organic carbon','E4/E6','E4_E6','-','E4_E6',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Fulvic to humic ratio (E4/E6), calculated between the absorption coefficient at 250 nm (a250) and the absorption coefficient at 365 nm (a365).	',1,'2021-10-25 15:59:45','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(55,52,'Dissolved organic carbon','S275-295','S275_295','-','S275_295',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Spectral slope S275-295	',1,'2021-10-25 16:00:15','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(56,53,'Dissolved organic carbon','S350-400','S350_400','-','S350_400',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Spectral slope S350-400	',1,'2021-10-25 16:00:46','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(57,54,'Dissolved organic carbon','S300-700','S300_700','-','S300_700',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','Spectral slope S300-700	',1,'2021-10-25 16:01:19','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(58,55,'Dissolved organic carbon','SR','SR','-','SR',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','The slope ratio SR (S275–295/S350–400) has been linked to shifts in DOM molecular weight and photobleaching (Helms et al. 2008), with steeper slope ratios reflective of greater amounts of low molecular weight compounds.	',1,'2021-10-25 16:01:40','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(59,56,'Dissolved organic carbon','Peak A/Peak T','A_T','-','A_T',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','An indication of the amount of humic-like (recalcitrant) vs. fresh-like (labile) fluorescence in a sample [ratio of Peak A (ex260/em450) to Peak T (ex275/em304) intensity].	',1,'2021-10-25 16:02:05','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(60,57,'Dissolved organic carbon','Peak C/Peak A','C_A','-','C_A',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','An indication of the amount of humic-like vs. Fulvic-like fluorescence in a sample [ratio of Peak C (ex340/em440) to Peak A (ex260/em450) intensity].	',1,'2021-10-25 16:02:38','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(61,58,'Dissolved organic carbon','Peak C/Peak M','C_M','-','C_M',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','An indication of the amount of diagenetically altered (blue-shifted) fluorescence in a sample [ratio of Peak C (ex340/em440) to Peak M (ex300/em390) intensity].	',1,'2021-10-25 16:03:00','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(62,59,'Dissolved organic carbon','Peak C/Peak T','C_T','-','C_T',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','An indication of the amount of humic-like (recalcitrant) vs. fresh-like (labile) fluorescence in a sample [ratio of Peak C (ex340/em440) to Peak T (ex275/em304) intensity].	',1,'2021-10-25 16:03:28','2021-11-17 13:19:14'),(63,12,'Nutrients','Soluble reactive phosphorus [µg/L] (Quikchem)','SRP_FIA','µg/L','NUT_P_avg',NULL,NULL,'basicPlot','The labile form of phosphorus (P) used by plants and algae. Measured in the laboratory from water samples (triplicates).',1,'2021-11-17 13:12:04','2021-11-17 13:19:13');

